# Koyeb / any buildpack-style Python host reads this for the start command.
# Migrations run first, in the same process start, so the schema is always
# at head before the API accepts traffic — the app itself no longer calls
# create_all (see app/main.py). Single instance by design, so there is no
# concurrent-migration race to worry about.
#
# Deliberately NOT passing --proxy-headers / --forwarded-allow-ips='*'.
# With those flags uvicorn rewrites request.client.host from the *leftmost*
# X-Forwarded-For entry (uvicorn/middleware/proxy_headers.py takes
# x_forwarded_for_hosts[0] when every host is trusted), and that entry is
# whatever the client sent. app/rate_limit.py._client_ip resolves the client
# itself from the right-hand side of the header via TRUSTED_PROXY_HOPS, and
# uses request.client.host only as a fallback — so letting uvicorn poison
# that fallback with attacker-controlled input would re-open the login
# limiter bypass the moment TRUSTED_PROXY_HOPS is set to 0. One source of
# truth for the client address, and it's the app's.
web: alembic upgrade head && uvicorn app.main:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port ${PORT:-8000}
